Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Open Binary Gibbs Energy Library: Cu-Ag Reference Reader", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"575d349e-7dd0-4bf1-94d1-dd8dcc935751"],

Cell["\<\
Development exemplar \[LongDash] this notebook is intended to demonstrate the \
current OBGEL JSON reader and will evolve with the schema and reference \
implementation.\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"42729dc2-ce3c-4156-a941-e56500cba972"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Purpose", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"66fde51d-82f2-47df-8320-5c80a299872c"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook demonstrates how the canonical OBGEL JSON representation is \
interpreted into symbolic Wolfram Language expressions. It uses the Cu-Ag FCC \
A1 phase as the first complete exemplar. The notebook is executable against \
the current repository data and is also intended to explain the construction \
of the thermodynamic model to future developers and teachers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f562b68-80df-4c26-a8d6-82c97d95060b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The main idea is simple: start with a useful Gibbs-energy function, then \
show how the JSON data are assembled into the expression. The thermodynamic \
structure is\n\n    ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["G", "TI"], "m"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["G", "TI"], "reference"], "+", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["G", "TI"], "ideal"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["G", "TI"], "empirical"]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "G_{\\mbox{m}} = G_{\\mbox{reference}} + \\Delta G_{\\mbox{ideal}}+ \
G_{\\mbox{empirical}}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a618e7dd-ada2-489b-b7e6-9d9554c3a9f4"],
 "\n\nFor the present Cu-Ag model, the empirical contribution is represented \
by a Redlich-Kister expansion. A future reader may expose a broader \
empiricalMixingContribution interface; this notebook deliberately uses only \
infrastructure that exists in the current repository."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9956894773245983`*^9, 3.995689478968616*^9}, 
   3.995689558381181*^9},ExpressionUUID->"799bfe49-a393-4831-97d4-\
4511ea10d5c1"],

Cell["\<\
The helper functions in this notebook are stored as initialization cells so \
that the examples can be evaluated from a fresh kernel.  If you accepted \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Evaluate Initialization Cells\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
then everything should work.

The notebook has been tested from a fresh Wolfram Language kernel with its \
initialization cells evaluated before the examples.\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.995714587903492*^9, 3.995714626077239*^9}, {
  3.995714897440207*^9, 
  3.995714899142482*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e1c232cc-5fe2-4236-8213-\
0039f2ca133f"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup and data loading", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1989ce1a-5c54-4706-b515-3f28f483c1ca"],

Cell["\<\
Run this section first. The path is derived from the notebook location so \
that the exemplar can live inside the repository without hard-coded \
user-specific paths.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b706a57-f70f-4256-9bba-b0df2bd5d0c1"],

